As far as I can remember what LFS was when I tried it a few years ago, the
NetBSD's build.sh script is some automatic process that does each steps
described in LFS' manual. When build.sh is finished, you have with
NetBSD what you get with LFS when you typed all the commands. In fact
you have much better things that with LFS but that's not the subject here
:)

NetBSD is also done well enough to "do it your-self" in certain cases.
Here's some notes (sorry comments in French) about how I
configured/installed one Ultra5 with RAID0 as root - no matter senses it
makes or not, I was just learning/playing with NetBSD RAIDframe ;)

