On Thu, Apr 27 2006 - 14:49, Hubert Feyrer wrote:
> On Thu, 27 Apr 2006, sp4rc wrote:
> >I have been googling for a while and came across FreeBSD from scratch
> >(apart from LFS) which raised my attention. Now I am wondering if there
> >is some documentation out there describing the same for NetBSD. Or has
> >someone experience with this and is willing to share his/her
> >documentation's?
>=20
> 	cd src
> 	./build.sh -m {sparc,alpha} tools release
>=20
> Sorry to burst your bubble, but that's NetBSD: We are no "distribution"=
=20
> that someone arranged, but a real operating system where everything comes=
=20
> from one source tree. The above compiles all of NetBSD into a=20
> ready-to-install release format.
>=20

As far as I can remember what LFS was when I tried it a few years ago, the
NetBSD's build.sh script is some automatic process that does each steps
described in LFS' manual. When build.sh is finished, you have with
NetBSD what you get with LFS when you typed all the commands. In fact
you have much better things that with LFS but that's not the subject here
:)

NetBSD is also done well enough to "do it your-self" in certain cases.
Here's some notes (sorry comments in French) about how I
configured/installed one Ultra5 with RAID0 as root - no matter senses it
makes or not, I was just learning/playing with NetBSD RAIDframe ;)

Note that those notes aren't really "NetBSD From Scratch" but more
"NetBSD from binaries, without the installer" ;)


